Hello, our name is Customertimes, but you can call us CT. We are a global digital engineering, product development, and technology consulting company. Headquartered in New York, we have a team of 1000+ experts working across 65+ countries. 

About this job: 

We are looking for an experienced QA Engineer with hands-on experience testing IQVIA OCE (Orchestrated Customer Engagement) applications. The ideal candidate should have strong functional testing, API testing, database validation, and automation experience, preferably within the pharmaceutical or life sciences domain. 

The candidate will be responsible for ensuring the quality, reliability, and performance of IQVIA OCE applications, including CRM workflows, integrations, data synchronization, and business processes. 

Location: India

Work Mode: Remote / Hybrid (depending on project requirements)

Employment Type: Full-time

How you'll make an impact: 

- Perform functional, regression, integration, system, and end-to-end testing of IQVIA OCE applications; 
 - Validate IQVIA OCE CRM functionalities, including HCP/HCO management, customer interactions, call planning, territory management, and sample management; 
 - Test OCE workflows, business rules, configurations, and customizations; 
 - Validate integrations between IQVIA OCE and external systems using REST APIs and other integration mechanisms; 
 - Perform database validation using SQL queries to ensure data accuracy and consistency; 
 - Create and maintain test plans, test scenarios, test cases, and test execution reports; 
 - Identify, document, track, and manage defects using Jira or similar tools; 
 - Collaborate with developers, business analysts, and product teams to understand requirements and resolve issues; 
 - Perform automation testing using Selenium, Playwright, or other automation frameworks; 
 - Participate in UAT, release validation, and production support testing; 
 - Ensure application quality, data integrity, and compliance with pharmaceutical industry requirements. 

Mandatory skills: 

- Hands-on experience in IQVIA OCE application testing; 
 - Strong functional and manual testing experience; 
 - Experience testing CRM applications and business workflows; 
 - Good understanding of pharmaceutical or life sciences domain processes; 
 - Experience in API testing using Postman or similar tools; 
 - Strong SQL and database validation skills; 
 - Experience in regression, integration, and end-to-end testing; 
 - Good knowledge of defect management and test documentation; 
 - Ability to independently create test scenarios and execute test cases. 

You are a star if you have: 

- Automation testing experience using Selenium, Playwright, or Cypress; 
 - Programming knowledge in Java, Python, or JavaScript; 
 - Experience with CI/CD pipelines; 
 - Knowledge of Salesforce CRM and its underlying architecture; 
 - Experience with IQVIA OCE configurations, customizations, and integrations; 
 - Experience in Veeva CRM or other pharmaceutical CRM platforms; 
 - Knowledge of pharmaceutical commercial operations and HCP engagement workflows. 

Required experience: 

Candidates must have practical project experience testing IQVIA OCE applications. General Salesforce CRM, Veeva CRM, or healthcare application testing without actual IQVIA OCE exposure will not be considered equivalent. 

If you're looking to contribute to global projects, grow your skills, shape the way you work, and be part of a connected international community - Customertimes is the place to build your next career chapter. Are you ready to spark the tech with us?

